#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:21
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:27
msgid "cookie.parse(str, options)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:29
msgid ""
"Parse an HTTP `Cookie` header string and returning an object of all "
"cookie name-value pairs. The `str` argument is the string representing a "
"`Cookie` header value and `options` is an optional object containing "
"additional parsing options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:38 ../../source/cookie_README.md:65
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:40
msgid "`cookie.parse` accepts these properties in the options object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:42
msgid "decode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:44
msgid ""
"Specifies a function that will be used to decode a cookie's value. Since "
"the value of a cookie has a limited character set (and must be a simple "
"string), this function can be used to decode a previously-encoded cookie "
"value into a JavaScript string or other object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:48
msgid ""
"The default function is the global `decodeURIComponent`, which will "
"decode any URL-encoded sequences into their byte representations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:51
msgid ""
"**note** if an error is thrown from this function, the original, non-"
"decoded cookie value will be returned as the cookie's value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:54
msgid "cookie.serialize(name, value, options)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:56
msgid ""
"Serialize a cookie name-value pair into a `Set-Cookie` header string. The"
" `name` argument is the name for the cookie, the `value` argument is the "
"value to set the cookie to, and the `options` argument is an optional "
"object containing additional serialization options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:67
msgid "`cookie.serialize` accepts these properties in the options object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:69
msgid "domain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:71
msgid ""
"Specifies the value for the [`Domain` `Set-Cookie` "
"attribute][rfc-6265-5.2.3]. By default, no domain is set, and most "
"clients will consider the cookie to apply to only the current domain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:74
msgid "encode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:76
msgid ""
"Specifies a function that will be used to encode a cookie's value. Since "
"value of a cookie has a limited character set (and must be a simple "
"string), this function can be used to encode a value into a string suited"
" for a cookie's value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:80
msgid ""
"The default function is the global `encodeURIComponent`, which will "
"encode a JavaScript string into UTF-8 byte sequences and then URL-encode "
"any that fall outside of the cookie range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:83
msgid "expires"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:85
msgid ""
"Specifies the `Date` object to be the value for the [`Expires` `Set-"
"Cookie` attribute][rfc-6265-5.2.1]. By default, no expiration is set, and"
" most clients will consider this a \"non-persistent cookie\" and will "
"delete it on a condition like exiting a web browser application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:89 ../../source/cookie_README.md:106
msgid ""
"**note** the [cookie storage model specification][rfc-6265-5.3] states "
"that if both `expires` and `maxAge` are set, then `maxAge` takes "
"precedence, but it is possible not all clients by obey this, so if both "
"are set, they should point to the same date and time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:93
msgid "httpOnly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:95
msgid ""
"Specifies the `boolean` value for the [`HttpOnly` `Set-Cookie` "
"attribute][rfc-6265-5.2.6]. When truthy, the `HttpOnly` attribute is set,"
" otherwise it is not. By default, the `HttpOnly` attribute is not set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:98
msgid ""
"**note** be careful when setting this to `true`, as compliant clients "
"will not allow client-side JavaScript to see the cookie in "
"`document.cookie`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:101
msgid "maxAge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:103
msgid ""
"Specifies the `number` (in seconds) to be the value for the [`Max-Age` "
"`Set-Cookie` attribute][rfc-6265-5.2.2]. The given number will be "
"converted to an integer by rounding down. By default, no maximum age is "
"set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:110
msgid "partitioned"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:112
msgid ""
"Specifies the `boolean` value for the [`Partitioned` `Set-Cookie`](rfc-"
"cutler-httpbis-partitioned-cookies) attribute. When truthy, the "
"`Partitioned` attribute is set, otherwise it is not. By default, the "
"`Partitioned` attribute is not set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:116 ../../source/cookie_README.md:137
#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:153
msgid ""
"**note** This is an attribute that has not yet been fully standardized, "
"and may change in the future. This also means many clients may ignore "
"this attribute until they understand it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:119
msgid ""
"More information about can be found in [the "
"proposal](https://github.com/privacycg/CHIPS)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:121
msgid "path"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:123
msgid ""
"Specifies the value for the [`Path` `Set-Cookie` "
"attribute][rfc-6265-5.2.4]. By default, the path is considered the "
"[\"default path\"][rfc-6265-5.1.4]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:126
msgid "priority"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:128
msgid ""
"Specifies the `string` to be the value for the [`Priority` `Set-Cookie` "
"attribute][rfc-west-cookie-priority-00-4.1]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:130
msgid "`'low'` will set the `Priority` attribute to `Low`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:131
msgid ""
"`'medium'` will set the `Priority` attribute to `Medium`, the default "
"priority when not set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:132
msgid "`'high'` will set the `Priority` attribute to `High`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:134
msgid ""
"More information about the different priority levels can be found in [the"
" specification][rfc-west-cookie-priority-00-4.1]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:140
msgid "sameSite"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:142
msgid ""
"Specifies the `boolean` or `string` to be the value for the [`SameSite` "
"`Set-Cookie` attribute][rfc-6265bis-09-5.4.7]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:144
msgid ""
"`true` will set the `SameSite` attribute to `Strict` for strict same site"
" enforcement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:145
msgid "`false` will not set the `SameSite` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:146
msgid ""
"`'lax'` will set the `SameSite` attribute to `Lax` for lax same site "
"enforcement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:147
msgid ""
"`'none'` will set the `SameSite` attribute to `None` for an explicit "
"cross-site cookie."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:148
msgid ""
"`'strict'` will set the `SameSite` attribute to `Strict` for strict same "
"site enforcement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:150
msgid ""
"More information about the different enforcement levels can be found in "
"[the specification][rfc-6265bis-09-5.4.7]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:156
msgid "secure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:158
msgid ""
"Specifies the `boolean` value for the [`Secure` `Set-Cookie` "
"attribute][rfc-6265-5.2.5]. When truthy, the `Secure` attribute is set, "
"otherwise it is not. By default, the `Secure` attribute is not set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_README.md:161
msgid ""
"**note** be careful when setting this to `true`, as compliant clients "
"will not send the cookie back to the server in the future if the browser "
"does not have an HTTPS connection."
msgstr ""

